tring>,\n6: ): boolean => {\n7:   if (availabilitySettings.useRecommendedModels) {\n8:     return (recommendedModelIds?.size ?? 0) > 0;\n9:   }\n11:   return availabilitySettings.enabledAiModelIds.length > 0;\n12: };\n```\n- `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/ai/ai-models/utils/is-model-allowed.util.ts`\n```\n3: export type WorkspaceModelAvailabilitySettings = {\n4:   useRecommendedModels: boolean;\n5:   enabledAiModelIds: string[];\n6: };\n8: export const isModelAllowedByWorkspace = (modelId, availabilitySettings, recommendedModelIds?) ...\n```\n- Consumer: `AiModelRegistryService.validateModelAvailability` (registry lines 463-490) uses `workspaceHasEnabledModels` for auto-select and `isModelAllowedByWorkspace` otherwise.\n- There is **no** `isAiEnabled`, `getEnabledModels`, or `hasProvider` predicate/method. The closest primitives are `workspaceHasEnabledModels` (availability settings only — it does not check that a provider is actually configured) and `AiModelRegistryService.hasTranscriptionModel()` (line 275).\n- `enabledAiModelIds` / `useRecommendedModels` live on `WorkspaceEntity` (`workspace.entity.ts:348` and `:352`) and are exposed by `workspace.resolver.ts:230` (`enabledAiModelIds`) and `:237` (`useRecommendedModels`).\n- `AI_PROVIDERS` is a config variable defaulting to `{}`: `config-variables.ts:1898`.\n- Instance client model list: `client-config.service.ts:65-108` builds `aiModels` from `aiModelRegistryService.getAdminFilteredModels()` (instance-wide, admin-disabled filter only, no workspace filter); `client-config.entity.ts:42` `ClientAiModelConfig`.\n\n## 5. Syna slash gating on the front\n\n`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/blocknote-editor/components/SynaSlashMenuItem.tsx` (69 lines):\n```\n27: export const SynaSlashMenuItem = ({ children }: SynaSlashMenuItemProps) => {\n28:   const hasAiPermissionFlag = useHasPermissionFlag(PermissionFlagType.AI);\n29:   const { enabledModels } = useWorkspaceAiModelAvailability();\n30:\n31:   if (!hasAiPermissionFlag || enabledModels.length === 0) {\n32:     return children([]);\n33:   }\n35:   return <SynaSlashMenuItemContent>{children}</SynaSlashMenuItemContent>;\n36: };\n```\nOuter gate intentionally prevents mounting `useContextToolButtons` (tool-index fetch) in zero-AI mode (comment lines 23-26). Inner component calls `getOfferedSynaActions({ actions: SYNA_DOCUMENT_AI_ACTIONS, hasAiPermissionFlag: true, hasAvailableModel: true, availableReadOnlyToolNames })` (lines 49-53) and stages a PREFILL draft (lines 60-65). Mounted in `BlockEditor.tsx:319-357`.\n\n`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ai/utils/getOfferedSynaActions.ts` (33 lines):\n```\n10: export const getOfferedSynaActions = ({ actions, hasAiPermissionFlag, hasAvailableModel, availableReadOnlyToolNames }: {...}): SynaAiAction[] => {\n21:   if (!hasAiPermissionFlag || !hasAvailableModel) {\n22:     return [];\n23:   }\n25:   return actions.filter(\n26:     (action) =>\n27:       action.readOnly &&\n28:       action.requiredToolNames.length > 0 &&\n29:       action.requiredToolNames.some((toolName) =>\n30:         availableReadOnlyToolNames.has(toolName),\n31:       ),\n32:   );\n33: };\n```\n\n`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ai/hooks/useWorkspaceAiModelAvailability.ts` (27 lines) — this is the front \"enabled models\" derivation (no dedicated query):\n```\n7: export const useWorkspaceAiModelAvailability = () => {\n8:   const aiModels = useAtomStateValue(aiModelsState);\n9:   const currentWorkspace = useAtomStateValue(currentWorkspaceState);\n11:   const useRecommendedModels = currentWorkspace?.useRecommendedModels ?? true;\n12:   const enabledAiModelIds = new Set(currentWorkspace?.enabledAiModelIds ?? []);\n14:   const realModels = aiModels.filter(\n15:     (model) => !isAutoSelectModelId(model.modelId) && !model.isDeprecated,\n16:   );\n18:   const enabledModels = useRecommendedModels\n19:     ? realModels.filter((model) => model.isRecommended === true)\n20:     : realModels.filter((model) => enabledAiModelIds.has(model.modelId));\n22:   return { enabledModels, realModels, useRecommendedModels };\n23: };\n```\n`aiModelsState` (`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/client-config/states/aiModelsState.ts:4`, typed `ClientAiModelConfig[]`) is populated by `useClientConfig.ts:181` (`setAiModels(clientConfig.aiModels ?? [])`) from the client-config REST payload (`ClientConfig.ts:17`). There is no GraphQL query named `enabledModels`; workspace scoping is applied client-side from `currentWorkspace`.\n\nRelated gates: `useAgentChat.ts:87` (`if (enabledModels.length === 0)` enqueues \"No AI models are enabled in this workspace.\"), `AiChatEditorSection.tsx:152-153,193,221,229`, `AiChatQuestionCard.tsx:231-232,524`, `AgentChatThreadInitializationEffect.tsx:38`, `MobileHomePage.tsx:32,49`, `MainNavigationDrawerContent.tsx:12,17-26`.\n\n## 6. Cmd+K \"Ask Syna\" (`EngineComponentKey.ASK_AI`, `askAi` constant) — definition and gating\n\nServer seed definition: `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/twenty-standard-application/constants/standard-command-menu-item.constant.ts`, exported `STANDARD_COMMAND_MENU_ITEMS` (line 8):\n```\n870:   askAi: {\n871:     universalIdentifier: 'ce5fb54d-2b19-4dd1-b7b4-9532a1761a41',\n873:     label: i18nLabel(msg({ message: `Ask AI`, context: 'commandMenuItem.label' })),\n875:     icon: 'IconMessageCirclePlus',\n876:     isPinned: true,\n877:     position: 43,\n879:     availabilityType: CommandMenuItemAvailabilityType.GLOBAL,\n880:     conditionalAvailabilityExpression:\n881:       'permissionFlags.AI and not isInSidePanel',\n884:     engineComponentKey: EngineComponentKey.ASK_AI,\n885:     hotKeys: ['@'],\n886:   },\n887:   viewPreviousAiChats: {\n...\n905:     conditionalAvailabilityExpression: 'permissionFlags.AI',\n908:     engineComponentKey: EngineComponentKey.VIEW_PREVIOUS_AI_CHATS,\n```\nEngine key enum: `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/command-menu-item/enums/engine-component-key.enum.ts:47` (`ASK_AI`), `:48` (`VIEW_PREVIOUS_AI_CHATS`). Front enum: `packages/twenty-front/src/generated-metadata/graphql.ts:1759`.\n\nHeadless mapping (what the command actually opens): `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu-item/engine-command/constants/EngineComponentKeyHeadlessComponentMap.tsx:213-219`:\n```\n213:   [EngineComponentKey.ASK_AI]: (\n214:     <HeadlessOpenSidePanelPageEngineCommand\n215:       page={SidePanelPages.AskAI}\n216:       pageTitle={msg`Syna`}\n217:       pageIcon={IconSparkles}\n218:     />\n219:   ),\n```\nGate evaluation: `useCurrentCommandMenuContextApi.ts:153-157` builds `permissionFlags` from `currentUserWorkspace?.permissionFlags`, then `CommandMenuContextProviderContent.tsx:61` and `StandalonePageCommandMenu.tsx:116` call `evaluateConditionalAvailabilityExpression(item.conditionalAvailabilityExpression, context)` (imported from `twenty-shared/utils`). So the effective gate is `permissionFlags.AI` (and `not isInSidePanel` for Ask AI).\n\nNote: the checked-in front mock `mock-command-menu-items-data.ts:938-983` still shows the older expression `\"permissionFlags.AI\"` for both items (stale vs. the current seed which adds `and not isInSidePanel`).\n\n## 7. `GET_TOOL_INDEX` / `useContextToolButtons`\n\n- Query: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ai/graphql/queries/getToolIndex.ts:3-14` — `export const GET_TOOL_INDEX = gql\\`query GetToolIndex { getToolIndex { name label description category objectName icon } }\\``.\n- Hook: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ai/hooks/useGetToolIndex.ts:8-15` — `export const useGetToolIndex = () => { ... useQuery<GetToolIndexQuery>(GET_TOOL_INDEX) ... return { toolIndex, loading, error } }`.\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ai/hooks/useContextToolButtons.ts:16-78` — `export const useContextToolButtons = (): ContextToolButton[]`, combines `toolIndex` with `logicFunctions`, `installedApplications`, context object permissions, then `getContextToolButtons(...)` (`.../utils/getContextToolButtons.ts:130+`).\n