`SynaSlashMenuItem.tsx:28-31`).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Lingui usage pattern\n\nBoth `SettingsAiOverviewTab` and `SettingsAiProviders` use the **macro `t`** with tagged-template literals:\n\n```ts\n// SettingsAiOverviewTab.tsx:11\nimport { t } from '@lingui/core/macro';\n...\n<H2Title\n  title={t`At a glance`}\n  description={t`What's installed and being used in your workspace`}\n/>\n...\nenqueueErrorSnackBar({ message: t`Failed to save workspace instructions` });   // :73\n```\n\n```ts\n// SettingsAiProviders.tsx:3\nimport { t } from '@lingui/core/macro';\n...\nenqueueErrorSnackBar({ message: t`Unable to save the provider` });   // :123\nenqueueSuccessSnackBar({ message: t`Provider saved` });              // :118\ndescription={t`Add and test a provider key, then pick the default and fast model.`}  // :173\n```\n\nVariants in the same area:\n- `SettingsAiProviderForm.tsx` imports both `t` (`@lingui/core/macro`) and `Trans` (`@lingui/react/macro`).\n- Components needing runtime translation use `const { t } = useLingui();` (`@lingui/react/macro`) — e.g. `SettingsAgentSettingsTab.tsx:2,68`, `SettingsAgentToolsTable.tsx:9,47`.\n- `SettingsAiUsageUserDetail.tsx:10-18` uses `import { Trans, useLingui }` and `const { t: tLingui } = useLingui();`.\n- No `msg\\`` usage found in these files; the dominant pattern is `t\\`…\\`` macro (zero-arg interpolation works inline, e.g. `t\\`${providerStatus.availableModelCount} models available\\``).\n\n---\n\n## 5. `SettingsPath` enum & how `AiProviders` was added\n\n**`packages/twenty-shared/src/types/SettingsPath.ts`** (relevant block, lines 40–49):\n\n```ts\nexport enum SettingsPath {\n  ...\n  AI = 'ai',\n  AiProviders = 'ai/providers',\n  AiUsageUserDetail = 'ai/usage/user/:userWorkspaceId',\n  AiPrompts = 'ai/prompts',\n  AiNewAgent = 'ai/new-agent',\n  AiAgentDetail = 'ai/agents/:agentId',\n  AiAgentTurnDetail = 'ai/agents/:agentId/turns/:turnId',\n  AiNewSkill = 'ai/new-skill',\n  AiSkillDetail = 'ai/skills/:skillId',\n  AiToolDetail = 