      "result": "<task id=\"ses_f0b9970bdffeUwdOxJtAt3e1KG\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI have completed a thorough exploration. Here is the complete map.\n\n---\n\n# A2E Suite — AI usage / event-log + billing surface map\n\n## 0. Context (why these surfaces exist)\n\n- **P9.1** (`PLAN.md:2098`) — \"Registry & assistant\", includes `[x] Streaming responses …, usage logging to event-logs` (`PLAN.md:2154`).\n- **US-045** = \"Audit page: Settings → AI (usage, logs, provider keys)\" (`PLAN.md:2265`). Verified, read-only Audit tab; AI usage via the event-logs table with entitlement gating.\n- **US-041** added the `ai-billing.service.spec.ts` proof (`PLAN.md:2156`, `docs/plan/phases/phase-01-report.md:1037`).\n- **US-130 / M10d** (`tasks/prd.json:602`, `PLAN.md:400`) — the *not-yet-built* \"per-workspace monthly token cap\"; acceptance says \"reuse event-logs usage from P9.1\" and explicitly \"no new billing backend\". `passes: false`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Event-logs usage surface (server)\n\n### Log table enum + registry\n- **`packages/twenty-shared/src/types/EventLogTable.ts:1`**\n  ```ts\n  export enum EventLogTable {\n    WORKSPACE_EVENT = 'WORKSPACE_EVENT',\n    PAGEVIEW = 'PAGEVIEW',\n    OBJECT_EVENT = 'OBJECT_EVENT',\n    USAGE_EVENT = 'USAGE_EVENT',\n    APPLICATION_LOG = 'APPLICATION_LOG',\n  }\n  ```\n- **`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/event-logs/registry/event-log-registry.ts:46-109`** — `EVENT_LOG_TYPES: Record<EventLogTable, EventLogTypeDefinition>`. Definition type has `{ clickHouseTable, requiresEntitlement, eventFieldName, normalize }` (lines 20-29).\n  - `USAGE_EVENT` (lines 65-86): `clickHouseTable: 'usageEvent'`, `requiresEntitlement: BillingEntitlementKey.AUDIT_LOGS`, `eventFieldName: 'resourceType'`, `normalize` maps `event=resourceType`, `userId=userWorkspaceId`, and `properties = { ...metadata, operationType, quantity, unit, creditsUsedMicro, resourceId, resourceContext }`.\n  - Other tables: `workspaceEvent`, `pageview`, `objectEvent` (all `AUDIT_LOGS`), `applicationLog` (`requiresEntitlement: null`).\n  - `getClickHouseTableName(table)` at line 108.\n\n### Usage row type (what a row carries)\n- **`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/event-logs/types/workspace-event-envelope.type.ts:28-41`**\n  ```ts\n  export type UsageEventRow = {\n    timestamp: string; workspaceId: string; periodStart?: string;\n    userWorkspaceId: string; resourceType: string; operationType: string;\n    quantity: number; unit: string; creditsUsedMicro: number;\n    resourceId: string; resourceContext: string; metadata: Record<string, unknown>;\n  };\n  ```\n- Envelope union `WorkspaceEventEnvelope` (line 55) includes `{ table: 'usageEvent'; row: UsageEventRow }`.\n\n### Enums\n- **`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/usage/enums/usage-operation-type.enum.ts:5-21`** — `UsageOperationType`: `ALL, AI_CHAT_TOKEN, AI_WORKFLOW_TOKEN, WORKFLOW_EXECUTION, CODE_EXECUTION, WEB_SEARCH, CALL_RECORDING, EMAIL_SEND, API_REQUEST, SUBSCRIPTION`. Registered as GraphQL enum name `UsageOperationType` (line 23).\n- **`…/usage/enums/usage-resource-type.enum.ts:5`** — `UsageResourceType`: `AI, WORKFLOW, APP, STORAGE, API, LOGIC_FUNCTION, EMAIL`.\n- **`…/usage/enums/usage-unit.enum.ts:3`** — `UsageUnit`: `CREDIT, TOKEN, INVOCATION, MINUTE, MILLISECOND, BYTE, REQUEST, SEAT`.\n- Shared app-facing subset: **`packages/twenty-shared/src/application/usageOperationTypesType.ts:5`** `USAGE_OPERATION_TYPES` (excludes `API_REQUEST`, `SUBSCRIPTION`).\n\n### ClickHouse physical table\n- Create: **`packages/twenty-server/src/database/clickhouse/migrations/004-create-usage-event-table.sql:1`**.\n- Current shape: **`006-update-usage-event-table.sql:1-21`** — `usageEvent` columns: `timestamp DateTime64(3)`, `workspaceId String`, `periodStart DateTime64(3)`, `userWorkspaceId String DEFAULT ''`, `resourceType LowCardinality(String)`, `operationType LowCardinality(String)`, `quantity Int64`, `unit LowCardinality(String) DEFAULT 'CREDIT'`, `creditsUsedMicro Int64`, `resourceId String`, `resourceContext String`, `metadata JSON`. `ORDER BY (workspaceId, timestamp, userWorkspaceId)`, TTL 3 YEAR. Adds projection `billing_by_workspace_period` (lines 46-53).\n- **`007-add-spender-columns-to-usage-event.sql:1-9`** adds `apiKeyId, applicationId, agentId, workflowId, logicFunctionId` (all `String DEFAULT ''`).\n- **`008-add-consumption-by-scope-daily-projection.sql:3`** adds projection `consumption_by_scope` grouped by workspace/resourceType/day/operation + every spender column, summing `creditsUsedMicro` and `quantity`.\n\n### Write path (how rows get written)\n1. **`UsageRecorderService`** — `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/usage/services/usage-recorder.service.ts`\n   - `record(workspaceId: string, inputs: RecordUsageInput[]): Promise<void>` (line 68): no-op if event sink disabled; stamps `periodStart` from `CreditAllowanceProvider.getCreditAllowancePeriod`; calls `WorkspaceEventEmitter.emitCustomBatchEvent<UsageEvent>(USAGE_RECORDED, …)` (line 75).\n   - `accumulate(workspaceId, input)` (line 85): buffers/rolls up via `UsageRollupBuffer`, flushes periodically (`USAGE_ROLLUP_FLUSH_INTERVAL_MS`).\n   - `withDefaults` (line 160) clamps invalid credit amounts to 0; `USAGE_RECORDED = 'USAGE_RECORDED'` (`…/usage/constants/usage-recorded.constant.ts:3`).\n2. **`UsageEventListener`** — `…/usage/listeners/usage-event.listener.ts:22` `@OnCustomBatchEvent(USAGE_RECORDED) handleUsageRecordedEvent` → `eventLogEmitterService.dispatch(buildUsageEventEnvelopes(...))`.\n3. **`buildUsageEventEnvelopes(workspaceId, usageEvents)`** — `…/usage/utils/build-usage-event-envelopes.ts:7` maps `UsageEvent` → `{ table: 'usageEvent', row: {… spender columns …} }`.\n4. **`EventLogEmitterService.dispatch(events)`** — `…/event-logs/emit/event-log-emitter.service.ts:32` → `WorkspaceEventSinkService.ingest`.\n5. **`WorkspaceEventSinkService.ingest`** — `…/event-logs/ingest/workspace-event-sink.service.ts:22` persists via sinks then `publishWatched` (live subscription).\n6. **`ClickHouseEventSink.write`** — `…/event-logs/ingest/clickhouse-event.sink.ts:25` groups rows by table and `clickHouseService.insert(table, rows, …)`.\n\n### Read path\n- **`EventLogsService.queryEventLogs(workspaceId, input)`** — `…/event-logs/event-logs.service.ts:43`; builds a raw ClickHouse `SELECT * FROM ${tableName} WHERE workspaceId … ORDER BY timestamp DESC LIMIT` (lines 88-101), entitlements via `validateAccess` (line 127: ClickHouse configured + `enterprisePlanService.isValid()` + `billingService.hasEntitlement(workspaceId, AUDIT_LOGS)`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. `AiBillingService` — cost/usage computation and writes\n\n**Path:** `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/ai/ai-billing/services/ai-billing.service.ts`\n\nConstructor deps (lines 27-31): `UsageRecorderService`, `AiModelRegistryService`, `BillingUsageService`.\n\nMethods (exact signatures):\n- `assertAiExecutionAllowed({ workspaceId, operationType, spenders }: { workspaceId: string; operationType: UsageOperationType; spenders: UsageSpenders }): Promise<void>` — line 33; delegates to `billingUsageService.assertUsageAllowed` with `resourceType: UsageResourceType.AI`.\n- `calculateCost(modelId: ModelId, billingInput: BillingUsageInput): number` — line 70. `BillingUsageInput = { usage: LanguageModelUsage; cacheCreationTokens?: number }` (line 18). Uses registry model config + `computeCostBreakdown`, logs and returns `totalCostInDollars`.\n- `calculateAndBillUsage(modelId, billingInput, workspaceId, operationType, agentId?, userWorkspaceId?): Promise<void>` — line 94. Computes cost → `creditsUsedMicro = convertDollarsToCreditsMicro`, `totalTokens = inputTokens + outputTokens`; `consumeQuota({ creditsUsedMicro, quantity: totalTokens })`; then `emitAiTokenUsageEvent(...)`.\n- `decrementAndCheckAvailableCredits({ modelId, billingInput, workspaceId, operationType, spenders }): Promise<{ hasNoMoreAvailableCredits: boolean }>` — line 127. Per-step quota consumption (does **not** write a usage event itself).\n- `billNativeWebSearchUsage(nativeWebSearchCallCount, workspaceId, userWorkspaceId?): Promise<void>` — line 155. No-op if count ≤ 0. Cost = `count * NATIVE_WEB_SEARCH_COST_PER_CALL_DOLLARS`; `consumeQuota({ operationType: WEB_SEARCH, quantity: count })`; then `usageRecorderService.record(..., [{ resourceType: AI, operationType: WEB_SEARCH, unit: INVOCATION, … }])` (lines 179-188).\n- `emitAiTokenUsageEvent(workspaceId, creditsUsedMicro, totalTokens, modelId, operationType, agentId?, userWorkspaceId?): Promise<void>` — line 191. Writes one `usageRecorderService.record` row with `resourceType: AI`, `unit: TOKEN`, `resourceId: agentId||null`, `resourceContext: modelId`, spenders `{ userWorkspaceId, agentId }`.\n\nCost primitives:\n- **`…/ai-billing/utils/compute-cost-breakdown.util.ts:42`** `computeCostBreakdown(model, usage)` — handles Anthropic vs OpenAI reasoning-token semantics, cache read/write rates, long-context pricing threshold.\n- **`…/ai-billing/utils/convert-dollars-to-credits-micro.util.ts:3`** `Math.round(dollars * DOLLAR_TO_CREDIT_MULTIPLIER)`.\n- **`…/ai-billing/constants/dollar-to-credit-multiplier.ts:2`** `DOLLAR_TO_CREDIT_MULTIPLIER = 1_000_000` (comment: `$0.000001 = 1 credit`).\n- **`…/ai-billing/constants/native-web-search-cost-per-call-dollars.ts:3`** `NATIVE_WEB_SEARCH_COST_PER_CALL_DOLLARS = 0.01`.\n- Web-search count helper: `…/utils/count-native-web-search-calls-from-steps.util.ts` (tool name `web_search`).\n- Module: `…/ai-billing/ai-billing.module.ts` (providers/exports `AiBillingService`).\n\n**The enum:** `UsageOperationType` at `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/usage/enums/usage-operation-type.enum.ts` (values `AI_CHAT_TOKEN='AI_CHAT_TOKEN'` line 7, `WEB_SEARCH='WEB_SEARCH'` line 11). Front mirror in generated metadata (`graphql.ts:6588`).\n\n**Who writes rows / when:**\n- `chat-execution.service.ts` — after a turn: `emitAiTokenUsageEvent(..., AI_CHAT_TOKEN, null, userWorkspaceId)` (`:483-491`); native web-search billing `:495`; per-step quota-only `decrementAndCheckAvailableCredits` in `onStepFinish` (`:611-623`); repair-tool-call path (`repair-tool-call.util.ts:116` `calculateAndBillUsage`).\n- `agent-async-executor.service.ts` — `assertAiExecutionAllowed` `:280`; per-step `decrementAndCheckAvailableCredits` `:413`, `:518`; `calculateCost` `:554`, `:584`; `emitAiTokenUsageEvent` `:593`; `billNativeWebSearchUsage` `:603`.\n- `agent-title-generation.service.ts` — `assertAiExecutionAllowed` `:30`, `calculateAndBillUsage` `:72`.\n- `agent-chat.resolver.ts` — `assertAiExecutionAllowed` `:191`, `:307`, `:364`.\n- `ai-generate-text.controller.ts` — `assertAiExecutionAllowed` `:58`, `calculateAndBillUsage` `:101`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Front \"Audit tab\" + event-logs usage surface\n\n### Audit tab (Settings → AI / \"Syna\")\n- **`packages/twenty-front/src/pages/settings/ai/SettingsAI.tsx`** — tabs defined lines 40-71; `AUDIT` titled `t\\`Audit\\`` (line 68); rendered `{isAuditTab && <SettingsAiAuditTab />}` (line 146). Tab ids in `…/ai/constants/SettingsAiTabs.ts:9` (`AUDIT: 'audit'`, plus `USAGE: 'usage'`).\n- **`packages/twenty-front/src/pages/settings/ai/components/SettingsAiAuditTab.tsx`**\n  - Provider credentials mask section (lines 100-125) via `getAiProviderCredentialStatuses(aiModels)`.\n  - Usage logs: `useEventLogs({ table: EventLogTable.USAGE_EVENT, first: AI_AUDIT_LOG_PAGE_SIZE /*50*/ }, { skip: !canQueryUsageLogs })` (lines 35-41), where `canQueryUsageLogs = isClickHouseConfigured && hasAuditLogsEntitlement` (lines 28-35).\n  - Renders `EventLogResultsTable` with `selectedTable={EventLogTable.USAGE_EVENT}` (lines 89-95); \"Recorded AI calls\" count = `totalCount`.\n  - Gate: `BillingEntitlementKey.AUDIT_LOGS` from `currentWorkspace.billingEntitlements`; enterprise gate card on `NO_ENTITLEMENT`.\n- Test: `…/ai/components/__tests__/SettingsAiAuditTab.test.tsx` asserts `useEventLogs` called with `{ table: EventLogTable.USAGE_EVENT }` and provider masking.\n\n### Generic logs tab (Settings → General → \"Logs\")\n- **`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/event-logs/components/SettingsLogs.tsx:91`** — table selector over all `EventLogTable` values, filter UI, live subscription, defaults to `PAGEVIEW`. Mounted by `packages/twenty-front/src/pages/settings/general/SettingsGeneral.tsx:100` (tab `logs`, guarded by `PermissionFlagType.SECURITY`).\n\n### GraphQL query used\n- **`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/event-logs/graphql/queries/getEventLogs.ts:3`**\n  ```graphql\n  query EventLogs($input: EventLogQueryInput!) {\n    eventLogs(input: $input) {\n      records { event timestamp userId properties recordId objectMetadataId }\n      totalCount\n      pageInfo { endCursor hasNextPage }\n    }\n  }\n  ```\n- Hook `useEventLogs` — `…/event-logs/hooks/useQueryEventLogs.ts:19` (`useQuery(GET_EVENT_LOGS, { fetchPolicy: 'network-only' })`, cursor pagination via `loadMore`).\n- Live: `…/graphql/subscriptions/EventLogsLiveSubscription.ts:3` `subscription EventLogsLive($table: EventLogTable!)`; hook `useEventLogsLiveStream.ts`.\n- Column mapping for `USAGE_EVENT`: `…/event-logs/utils/getColumnsForEventLogTable.tsx:80-85` (`Resource Type`, `Timestamp`, `User`, `Details`).\n- Generated ops: `EventLogsDocument` → `packages/twenty-front/src/generated-metadata/graphql.ts:9891`, `EventLogsLiveDocument` → `:9892`, `GetUsageAnalyticsDocument` → `:9924`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Workspace-level credit / usage / quota / cap (already present)\n\n### Quota entity + config\n- **`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/usage-limit/usage-limit.entity.ts`** — `@Entity({ name: 'usageLimit', schema: 'core' })` (table `core.usageLimit`). Columns: `id`, `resourceType`, `operationType`, `spenderType`, `spenderId` (default `''`), `limitKind`, `periodCount`, `periodUnit`, `meter`, `limitValue bigint`, `burstValue bigint|null`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`; unique `UQ_USAGE_LIMIT_SCOPE`.\n- **`…/usage-limit/constants/usage-limit-definitions.constant.ts:38-54`** — the only quota definition is `UsageResourceType.AI`, allowed operations `AI_CHAT_TOKEN`, `AI_WORKFLOW_TOKEN`, `WEB_SEARCH`; spenders `workspace|userWorkspace|apiKey|application|agent`; meters `creditsUsedMicro|quantity`. This is the existing generic quota mechanism (not a bespoke \"monthly token cap\").\n- Periods: `…/usage-limit/services/usage-period.service.ts`; period units constant `…/constants/period-units.constant.ts`.\n\n### Services & signatures\n- **`UsageLimitService`** — `…/usage-limit/services/usage-limit.service.ts`\n  - `findAll(workspaceId): Promise<UsageLimitEntity[]>` (46)\n  - `upsert({ workspaceId, input: UpsertUsageLimitInput }): Promise<UsageLimitEntity>` (50) — validates against definition, requires intra-workspace entitlement, invalidates `usageLimits` workspace cache.\n  - `delete({ workspaceId, usageLimitId }): Promise<boolean>` (117).\n- **`UsageLimitQuotaService`** — `…/usage-limit/services/usage-limit-quota.service.ts`\n  - `assertQuotaNotExhausted(args: QuotaConsumeArgs): Promise<void>` (91)\n  - `consumeQuota({ cost, ...args }): Promise<{ exhausted: ExhaustedScope[] }>` (104)\n  - `getAllowanceRemainingMicro(workspaceId): Promise<number|null>` (195)\n  - reads `usageEvent` from ClickHouse to warm cold counters (`fetchAllowanceConsumedMicro:659`, `fetchConsumptionRows:707`).\n- **`UsageLimitEntitlementService`** — `…/usage-limit/services/usage-limit-entitlement.service.ts`\n  - `isIntraWorkspaceLimitEntitled(workspaceId): Promise<boolean>` (26)\n  - `findEnforceableLimits({ workspaceId, limits }): Promise<FlatUsageLimit[]>` (32) — fails open.\n- **`UsageLimitResolver`** — `…/usage-limit/usage-limit.resolver.ts` (guarded by `SettingsPermissionGuard(PermissionFlagType.WORKSPACE)`):\n  - `Query usageLimits: [UsageLimitDTO]` (33)\n  - `Mutation upsertUsageLimit(input: UpsertUsageLimitInput!): UsageLimitDTO` (42)\n  - `Mutation deleteUsageLimit(usageLimitId: UUID!): Boolean` (55).\n\n### Credit allowance / billing\n- **Interface** `CreditAllowanceProvider` — `…/usage-limit/interfaces/credit-allowance-provider.service.ts:7`\n  - `isCreditAllowanceEnabled(workspaceId): Promise<boolean>`\n  - `getCreditAllowancePeriod(workspaceId): Promise<UsagePeriod|null>`\n  - `getCreditAllowance(workspaceId): Promise<CreditAllowance|null>`\n  - discovery via `…/utils/find-credit-allowance-provider.util.ts`.\n- **Impl** `BillingCreditAllowanceProvider` — `…/billing/services/billing-credit-allowance-provider.service.ts:18`\n  - `getCreditAllowancePeriod` returns `{ periodStart, periodEnd }` from the cached subscription (35-55).\n  - `getCreditAllowance` returns `allowanceMicro = getResourceUsageCap(subscription) + getActiveCreditsMicro(workspaceId)` (74-83).\n- **`BillingUsageService`** — `…/billing/services/billing-usage.service.ts`\n  - `isAllowanceCounterEnabled(workspaceId): Promise<boolean>` (96) — feature flag `IS_QUOTA_ENGINE_CREDIT_BOUND_ENABLED`.\n  - `assertUsageAllowed({ workspaceId, resourceType, operationType, spenders }): Promise<void>` (112) — subscription active + available-credit check + quota check.\n  - `consumeUsageQuota(...): Promise<{ hasNoMoreAvailableCredits: boolean }>` (132).\n  - `getCreditAvailability(workspaceId): Promise<CreditAvailability>` (214) — reasons `NO_SUBSCRIPTION | WORKSPACE_SUSPENDED | NO_CREDITS`.\n  - `hasAvailableCredits(workspaceId): Promise<boolean>` (237).\n  - `getResourceCreditProductUsage(workspace): Promise<BillingResourceCreditUsageDTO[]>` (244).\n  - `getTrialResourceUsageCap(subscription)` (352); **`getResourceUsageCap(subscription): number`** (358) — reads `RESOURCE_CREDIT` price metadata `credit_amount`.\n  - `getCreditsUsedBetweenOrNull({workspaceId, from, to})` (561); `getCurrentPeriodCreditsUsed(workspaceId, periodStart)` (581) — both sum `creditsUsedMicro` from ClickHouse `usageEvent`.\n- **`BillingService`** — `…/billing/services/billing.service.ts` — `isBillingEnabled()` (30), `hasEntitlement(workspaceId, entitlementKey: BillingEntitlementKey)` (72).\n- **`BillingEntitlementKey`** — `…/billing/enums/billing-entitlement-key.enum.ts:3`: `SSO, CUSTOM_DOMAIN, RLS, AUDIT_LOGS, USAGE_LIMIT`.\n- **`BillingCreditGrantService`** (credit grants / rollover ledger, table `billingCreditGrant`) — `…/billing/services/billing-credit-grant.service.ts`: `createGrant(params): Promise<BillingCreditGrantEntity|null>` (71), `getActiveCreditsMicro(workspaceId): Promise<number>` (132), `findGrantsLiveDuringPeriod(...)` (159), `revokeGrant(...)` (230). Related: `billing-credit-rollover.service.ts`, `billing-credit.service.ts`, entity `entities/billing-credit-grant.entity.ts`.\n- **`CreditAllowance`** type — `…/usage-limit/types/credit-allowance.type.ts:3` = `UsagePeriod & { allowanceMicro: number }`.\n- Workspace-level retention (adjacent billing quota-ish setting): `workspace.entity.ts:147 eventLogRetentionDays` (default 90), settable/permission-gated via `workspace.service.ts:115` and `dtos/update-workspace-input.ts:115`.\n- Admin-panel billing: `AdminPanelWorkspaceBillingDTO` (`…/admin-panel/dtos/admin-panel-workspace-billing.dto.ts:7`) + `AdminBillingService.getWorkspaceBilling(workspaceId)` (`…/admin-panel/services/admin-panel-billing.service.ts:181`); resolver `adminPanel.resolver.ts:631`.\n\n> **Note on the still-missing piece (US-130):** there is no AI-specific \"monthly token cap\" entity/field today. The generic `usageLimit` quota (per resource/operation/spender/period, meter `quantity` or `creditsUsedMicro`) is the primitive to reuse, and the `usageEvent` ClickHouse rows (`AI_CHAT_TOKEN`/`WEB_SEARCH`) are the usage source.\n\n---\n\n## 5. GraphQL operations & DTOs exposing event logs / usage to the front\n\nServer resolvers:\n- **`EventLogsResolver`** — `…/event-logs/event-logs.resolver.ts:42` `@Query(() => EventLogQueryResult) eventLogs(input: EventLogQueryInput!)` guarded `WorkspaceAuthGuard + SettingsPermissionGuard(PermissionFlagType.SECURITY)`.\n- **`EventLogsLiveResolver`** —