        "result": "<task id=\"ses_f0b99712bffesh2evTOc4naiih\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI have completed a thorough exploration. Here is the map.\n\n# A2E Suite — AI provider resolution and zero-AI gating map\n\n## 1. `provider-config.service.ts` — US-102 resolution order\n\nPath: `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/ai/ai-models/services/provider-config.service.ts` (166 lines)\n\nExported class `ProviderConfigService` (line 15). Constructor deps: `TwentyConfigService`, `DefaultAiCatalogService`, `WorkspaceAiProviderService` (lines 17-21).\n\nExact signatures:\n- `getCatalogProviderNames(): Set<string>` — line 23\n- `getResolvedProviders({ includeCustomProviders = true }: { includeCustomProviders?: boolean } = {}): AiProvidersConfig` — line 29\n- `async getResolvedProvidersForWorkspace({ workspaceId, includeCustomProviders = true }: { workspaceId: string; includeCustomProviders?: boolean }): Promise<AiProvidersConfig>` — line 54\n- `private buildWorkspaceModelsForProvider({ baseProvider, workspaceProviderModels }: { baseProvider?: AiProviderConfig; workspaceProviderModels: Array<string | null> }): { models?: AiProviderModelConfig[] }` — line 94\n- `private resolveTemplates(providers: AiProvidersConfig): AiProvidersConfig` — line 118\n- `private resolveProviderTemplates(config: AiProviderConfig): AiProviderConfig` — line 128\n- `private resolveTemplate(value?: string): string | undefined` — line 138\n\nResolution order (comment lines 48-53, implementation 61-88):\n```\n48:   // Resolution order: workspace BYOK provider → instance AI_PROVIDERS →\n49:   // committed catalog. Workspace entries are merged last and never run through\n50:   // resolveTemplates ... They are also merged even when includeCustomProviders is\n51:   // false ... (D-N4).\n```\n`getResolvedProviders` resolves `{{VAR}}` templates only in the committed catalog, then merges instance `AI_PROVIDERS` (`this.twentyConfigService.get('AI_PROVIDERS')`, line 43). `getResolvedProvidersForWorkspace` starts from that and reduces `workspaceAiProviderService.resolveProviders(workspaceId)` (lines 64-65) on top: `{ ...baseProvider, ...workspaceProvider.providerConfig, ...buildWorkspaceModelsForProvider(...) }` (lines 73-82). Workspace models only become the model list when the base provider has no catalog `models` (lines 101-116).\n\nCritical finding: `getResolvedProvidersForWorkspace` has **no production caller**. Grep across the repo finds it only in the service itself, `__tests__/provider-config.service.spec.ts`, and `test/integration/ai/suites/workspace-ai-provider.integration-spec.ts`. The live registry (`AiModelRegistryService`) still uses instance-wide `getResolvedProviders()`.\n\n## 2. `AiModelRegistryService.buildModelRegistry` — instance-wide, not workspace-scoped\n\nPath: `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/ai/ai-models/services/ai-model-registry.service.ts` (593 lines)\n\nExported `interface RegisteredAiModel` (line 46), `type RegisteredAiTranscriptionModel` (line 55), class `AiModelRegistryService` (line 63).\n\n- `private ensureFresh(): void` — line 94. Rebuilds when `ConfigVariablesGroup.LLM` hash or custom-provider entitlement changes.\n- `private buildModelRegistry(areCustomProvidersAllowed: boolean): void` — line 113. Clears all caches then calls:\n```\n121:     const providers = this.providerConfigService.getResolvedProviders({\n122:       includeCustomProviders: areCustomProvidersAllowed,\n123:     });\n125:     this.registerModelsFromProviders(providers);\n```\nNo `workspaceId` parameter anywhere in this class — the registry is a single instance-wide `Map`, so workspace BYOK is **not** a generation-time consumer. Confirmed by `docs/plan/phases/phase-14-report.md:72` and `.ralph-tui/progress.md:276-277`.\n\nOther relevant signatures:\n- `private registerModelsFromProviders(providers: AiProvidersConfig): void` — line 128\n- `getModel(modelId: string): RegisteredAiModel | undefined` — 313\n- `getAvailableModels(): RegisteredAiModel[]` — 319\n- `getModelConfig(modelId: string): AiModelConfig | undefined` — 325\n- `getEffectiveModelConfig(modelId: string): AiModelConfig` — 378\n- `isModelAdminAllowed(modelId: string): boolean` — 452\n- `validateModelAvailability(modelId: string, availabilitySettings: WorkspaceModelAvailabilitySettings): void` — 463\n- `getAdminFilteredModels(): RegisteredAiModel[]` — 492\n- `getAllModelsWithStatus(): Array<{ modelConfig; isAvailable; isAdminEnabled; isRecommended; providerName?; name? }>` — 498\n- `getResolvedProvidersForAdmin(): AiProvidersConfig` — 569 (delegates to `getResolvedProviders()`)\n- `getCatalogProviderNames(): Set<string>` — 573\n- `hasTranscriptionModel(): boolean` — 275\n\n## 3. `workspace-ai-provider.service.ts` and entity\n\nPath: `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/ai/ai-models/services/workspace-ai-provider.service.ts` (199 lines)\n\nExported types:\n```\n19: export type ResolvedWorkspaceAiProvider = {\n20:   providerName: string;\n21:   providerConfig: AiProviderConfig;\n22:   defaultModel: string | null;\n23:   fastModel: string | null;\n24: };\n26: export type UpsertWorkspaceAiProviderInput = {\n27:   workspaceId: string; provider: string; npm: string; label?: string;\n28:   apiKey?: string; baseUrl?: string; defaultModel?: string; fastModel?: string;\n29: };\n```\nClass `WorkspaceAiProviderService` (line 38). Methods:\n- `async resolveProviders(workspaceId: string): Promise<ResolvedWorkspaceAiProvider[]>` — line 45 (decrypts each row via `toResolvedProvider`)\n- `async getProvider({ workspaceId, provider }: { workspaceId: string; provider: string }): Promise<WorkspaceAiProviderEntity | null>` — line 55\n- `async findProviders(workspaceId: string): Promise<WorkspaceAiProviderEntity[]>` — line 69 (raw rows, no decryption, ordered by `createdAt ASC`)\n- `decryptProviderApiKey(row: WorkspaceAiProviderEntity): string | undefined` — line 79\n- `async upsertProvider({...}: UpsertWorkspaceAiProviderInput): Promise<void>` — line 85\n- `async removeProvider({ workspaceId, provider }): Promise<void>` — line 143\n- private `toResolvedProvider` — 153, `decryptApiKeyOrThrow` — 180\n\nEntity: `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/ai/ai-models/entities/workspace-ai-provider.entity.ts`\n- `@Entity({ name: 'workspaceAiProvider', schema: 'core' })`, `@Unique('IDX_WORKSPACE_AI_PROVIDER_WORKSPACE_PROVIDER_UNIQUE', ['workspaceId','provider'])` (lines 15-19)\n- extends `WorkspaceRelatedEntity` (supplies `workspaceId`)\n- fields: `id` (uuid PK), `provider`, `npm`, `label: string|null`, `encryptedApiKey: string|null`, `baseUrl: string|null`, `defaultModel: string|null`, `fastModel: string|null`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`\n\nGraphQL surface (US-127): `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/ai/ai-models/resolvers/workspace-ai-provider.resolver.ts` — class `WorkspaceAiProviderResolver`, guarded by `WorkspaceAuthGuard` + `SettingsPermissionGuard(PermissionFlagType.AI_SETTINGS)` (lines 21-27). Query `workspaceAiProviders` (34), mutations `upsertWorkspaceAiProvider` (43), `testWorkspaceAiProvider` (58), `removeWorkspaceAiProvider` (69). All return `WorkspaceAiProvidersDTO` from `WorkspaceAiProviderAdminService.getProvidersOverview(workspaceId)`.\n\nImportant nuance: `WorkspaceAiProviderAdminService.getProvidersOverview` (`.../services/workspace-ai-provider-admin.service.ts:40`) uses the **instance** `getResolvedProviders({ includeCustomProviders: true })` (lines 43-45) plus `findProviders` raw rows (46-47); it advertises `resolutionOrder: [WORKSPACE, INSTANCE, CATALOG]` (66-70) but does not call `getResolvedProvidersForWorkspace`.\n\n## 4. Server-side \"does this workspace have AI / enabled models\" predicates\n\n- `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/ai/ai-models/utils/workspace-has-enabled-models.util.ts`\n```\n3: export const workspaceHasEnabledModels = (\n4:   availabilitySettings: WorkspaceModelAvailabilitySettings,\n5:   recommendedModelIds?: Set<string>,\n6: ): boolean => {\n7:   if (availabilitySettings.useRecommendedModels) {\n8:     return (recommendedModelIds?.size ?? 0) > 0;\n9:   }\n11:   return availabilitySettings.enabledAiModelIds.length > 0;\n12: };\n```\n- `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/ai/ai-models/utils/is-model-allowed.util.ts`\n```\n3: export type WorkspaceModelAvailabilitySettings = {\n4:   useRecommendedModels: boolean;\n5:   enabledAiModelIds: string[];\n6: };\n8: export const isModelAllowedByWorkspace = (modelId, availabilitySettings, recommendedModelIds?) ...\n```\n- Consumer: `AiModelRegistryService.validateModelAvailability` (registry lines 463-490) uses `workspaceHasEnabledModels` for auto-select and `isModelAllowedByWorkspace` otherwise.\n- There is **no** `isAiEnabled`, `getEnabledModels`, or `hasProvider` predicate/method. The closest primitives are `workspaceHasEnabledModels` (availability settings only — it does not check that a provider is actually configured) and `AiModelRegistryService.hasTranscriptionModel()` (line 275).\n- `enabledAiModelIds` / `useRecommendedModels` live on `WorkspaceEntity` (`workspace.entity.ts:348` and `:352`) and are exposed by `workspace.resolver.ts:230` (`enabledAiModelIds`) and `:237` (`useRecommendedModels`).\n- `AI_PROVIDERS` is a config variable defaulting to `{}`: `config-variables.ts:1898`.\n- Instance client model list: `client-config.service.ts:65-108` builds `aiModels` from `aiModelRegistryService.getAdminFilteredModels()` (instance-wide, admin-disabled filter only, no workspace filter); `client-config.entity.ts:42` `ClientAiModelConfig`.\n\n## 5. Syna slash gating on the front\n\n`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/blocknote-editor/components/SynaSlashMenuItem.tsx` (69 lines):\n```\n27: export const SynaSlashMenuItem = ({ children }: SynaSlashMenuItemProps) => {\n28:   const hasAiPermissionFlag = useHasPermissionFlag(PermissionFlagType.AI);\n29:   const { enabledModels } = useWorkspaceAiModelAvailability();\n30:\n31:   if (!hasAiPermissionFlag || enabledModels.length === 0) {\n32:     return children([]);\n33:   }\n35:   return <SynaSlashMenuItemContent>{children}</SynaSlashMenuItemContent>;\n36: };\n```\nOuter gate intentionally prevents mounting `useContextToolButtons` (tool-index fetch) in zero-AI mode (comment lines 23-26). Inner component calls `getOfferedSynaActions({ actions: SYNA_DOCUMENT_AI_ACTIONS, hasAiPermissionFlag: true, hasAvailableModel: true, availableReadOnlyToolNames })` (lines 49-53) and stages a PREFILL draft (lines 60-65). Mounted in `BlockEditor.tsx:319-357`.\n\n`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ai/utils/getOfferedSynaActions.ts` (33 lines):\n```\n10: export const getOfferedSynaActions = ({ actions, hasAiPermissionFlag, hasAvailableModel, availableReadOnlyToolNames }: {...}): SynaAiAction[] => {\n21:   if (!hasAiPermissionFlag || !hasAvailableModel) {\n22:     return [];\n23:   }\n25:   return actions.filter(\n26:     (action) =>\n27:       action.readOnly &&\n28:       action.requiredToolNames.length > 0 &&\n29:       action.requiredToolNames.some((toolName) =>\n30:         availableReadOnlyToolNames.has(toolName),\n31:       ),\n32:   );\n33: };\n```\n\n`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ai/hooks/useWorkspaceAiModelAvailability.ts` (27 lines) — this is the front \"enabled models\" derivation (no dedicated query):\n```\n7: export const useWorkspaceAiModelAvailability = () => {\n8:   const aiModels = useAtomStateValue(aiModelsState);\n9:   const currentWorkspace = useAtomStateValue(currentWorkspaceState);\n11:   const useRecommendedModels = currentWorkspace?.useRecommendedModels ?? true;\n12:   const enabledAiModelIds = new Set(currentWorkspace?.enabledAiModelIds ?? []);\n14:   const realModels = aiModels.filter(\n15:     (model) => !isAutoSelectModelId(model.modelId) && !model.isDeprecated,\n16:   );\n18:   const enabledModels = useRecommendedModels\n19:     ? realModels.filter((model) => model.isRecommended === true)\n20:     : realModels.filter((model) => enabledAiModelIds.has(model.modelId));\n22:   return { enabledModels, realModels, useRecommendedModels };\n23: };\n```\n`aiModelsState` (`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/client-config/states/aiModelsState.ts:4`, typed `ClientAiModelConfig[]`) is populated by `useClientConfig.ts:181` (`setAiModels(clientConfig.aiModels ?? [])`) from the client-config REST payload (`ClientConfig.ts:17`). There is no GraphQL query named `enabledModels`; workspace scoping is applied client-side from `currentWorkspace`.\n\nRelated gates: `useAgentChat.ts:87` (`if (enabledModels.length === 0)` enqueues \"No AI models are enabled in this workspace.\"), `AiChatEditorSection.tsx:152-153,193,221,229`, `AiChatQuestionCard.tsx:231-232,524`, `AgentChatThreadInitializationEffect.tsx:38`, `MobileHomePage.tsx:32,49`, `MainNavigationDrawerContent.tsx:12,17-26`.\n\n## 6. Cmd+K \"Ask Syna\" (`EngineComponentKey.ASK_AI`, `askAi` constant) — definition and gating\n\nServer seed definition: `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/twenty-standard-application/constants/standard-command-menu-item.constant.ts`, exported `STANDARD_COMMAND_MENU_ITEMS` (line 8):\n```\n870:   askAi: {\n871:     universalIdentifier: 'ce5fb54d-2b19-4dd1-b7b4-9532a1761a41',\n873:     label: i18nLabel(msg({ message: `Ask AI`, context: 'commandMenuItem.label' })),\n875:     icon: 'IconMessageCirclePlus',\n876:     isPinned: true,\n877:     position: 43,\n879:     availabilityType: CommandMenuItemAvailabilityType.GLOBAL,\n880:     conditionalAvailabilityExpression:\n881:       'permissionFlags.AI and not isInSidePanel',\n884:     engineComponentKey: EngineComponentKey.ASK_AI,\n885:     hotKeys: ['@'],\n886:   },\n887:   viewPreviousAiChats: {\n...\n905:     conditionalAvailabilityExpression: 'permissionFlags.AI',\n908:     engineComponentKey: EngineComponentKey.VIEW_PREVIOUS_AI_CHATS,\n```\nEngine key enum: `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/command-menu-item/enums/engine-component-key.enum.ts:47` (`ASK_AI`), `:48` (`VIEW_PREVIOUS_AI_CHATS`). Front enum: `packages/twenty-front/src/generated-metadata/graphql.ts:1759`.\n\nHeadless mapping (what the command actually opens): `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu-item/engine-command/constants/EngineComponentKeyHeadlessComponentMap.tsx:213-219`:\n```\n213:   [EngineComponentKey.ASK_AI]: (\n214:     <HeadlessOpenSidePanelPageEngineCommand\n215:       page={SidePanelPages.AskAI}\n216:       pageTitle={msg`Syna`}\n217:       pageIcon={IconSparkles}\n218:     />\n219:   ),\n```\nGate evaluation: `useCurrentCommandMenuContextApi.ts:153-157` builds `permissionFlags` from `currentUserWorkspace?.permissionFlags`, then `CommandMenuContextProviderContent.tsx:61` and `StandalonePageCommandMenu.tsx:116` call `evaluateConditionalAvailabilityExpression(item.conditionalAvailabilityExpression, context)` (imported from `twenty-shared/utils`). So the effective gate is `permissionFlags.AI` (and `not isInSidePanel` for Ask AI).\n\nNote: the checked-in front mock `mock-command-menu-items-data.ts:938-983` still shows the older expression `\"permissionFlags.AI\"` for both items (stale vs. the current seed which adds `and not isInSidePanel`).\n\n## 7. `GET_TOOL_INDEX` / `useContextToolButtons`\n\n- Query: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ai/graphql/queries/getToolIndex.ts:3-14` — `export const GET_TOOL_INDEX = gql\\`query GetToolIndex { getToolIndex { name label description category objectName icon } }\\``.\n- Hook: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ai/hooks/useGetToolIndex.ts:8-15` — `export const useGetToolIndex = () => { ... useQuery<GetToolIndexQuery>(GET_TOOL_INDEX) ... return { toolIndex, loading, error } }`.\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ai/hooks/useContextToolButtons.ts:16-78` — `export const useContextToolButtons = (): ContextToolButton[]`, combines `toolIndex` with `logicFunctions`, `installedApplications`, context object permissions, then `getContextToolButtons(...)` (`.../utils/getContextToolButtons.ts:130+`).\n- Server resolver: `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/tool-provider/resolvers/tool-index.resolver.ts` — `ToolIndexEntryDTO` (line 20), class `ToolIndexResolver` (45), `async getToolIndex(user, workspace, userWorkspaceId, locale): Promise<ToolIndexEntryDTO[]>` (53-73), guarded by `@UseGuards(NoPermissionGuard)` (52). Delegates to `toolRegistryService.buildToolIndex(workspace.id, roleId, {...})` (68). `getToolIndex` itself is not AI-gated; the Syna component gate (section 5) is what prevents the fetch in zero-AI mode.\n\n## Summary of the zero-AI state\n\n- Server provider resolution: `ProviderConfigService.getResolvedProviders` (catalog + instance `AI_PROVIDERS`) is the only path feeding `AiModelRegistryService.buildModelRegistry`; the US-102 workspace BYOK path `getResolvedProvidersForWorkspace` exists but is unwired outside tests (no generation-time consumer).\n- No server `isAiEnabled`/`hasProvider` predicate. Zero-AI availability is expressed as `workspaceHasEnabledModels` / `isModelAllowedByWorkspace` against workspace `useRecommendedModels` + `enabledAiModelIds`, plus the registry's model list (which is empty when no provider is configured).\n- Front zero-AI gating is consistently `useHasPermissionFlag(PermissionFlagType.AI)` AND `enabledModels.length > 0`, where `enabledModels` is derived from client config `aiModels` filtered by `currentWorkspace.useRecommendedModels` / `enabledAiModelIds`. Cmd+K entries gate on `permissionFlags.AI` (with `and not isInSidePanel` for `ASK_AI`) evaluated from `currentUserWorkspace.permissionFlags`.\n\nNo files were modified.\n</task_result>\n</task>"
