        "result": "<task id=\"ses_f0b997093ffePsBUslgz3zVbWg\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\n# A2E Suite — Settings → Syna & Front AI Surfaces Map\n\n## 1. Settings → Syna tab (`SettingsPath.AI` = `ai`)\n\n### Tab registration & page\n- **`packages/twenty-front/src/pages/settings/ai/SettingsAI.tsx`** — `export const SettingsAI` (line 37). The Syna settings page; title `t\\`Syna\\`` (line 87). Uses `SettingsPageLayout` + `SettingsTabBar` + `useSettingsActiveTabId`.\n- **`packages/twenty-front/src/pages/settings/ai/constants/SettingsAiTabs.ts`** — `SETTINGS_AI_TABS`:\n```ts\nexport const SETTINGS_AI_TABS = {\n  COMPONENT_INSTANCE_ID: 'settings-ai-tab-list',\n  TABS_IDS: {\n    OVERVIEW: 'overview', MODELS: 'models', SKILLS: 'skills',\n    TOOLS: 'tools', USAGE: 'usage', AUDIT: 'audit',\n  },\n} as const;\n```\n\n**Tabs that exist** (SettingsAI.tsx lines 40–71, rendered lines 141–146):\n\n| Tab id | Title | Component | File |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `overview` | Overview | `SettingsAiOverviewTab` | `pages/settings/ai/components/SettingsAiOverviewTab.tsx` |\n| `models` | Models | `SettingsAiModelsTab` | `.../components/SettingsAiModelsTab.tsx` |\n| `skills` | Skills | `SettingsAgentSkillsTab` | `.../components/SettingsAgentSkillsTab.tsx` |\n| `tools` | Tools | `SettingsAgentToolsTab` | `.../components/SettingsAgentToolsTab.tsx` |\n| `usage` | Usage | `SettingsAiUsageTab` | `.../components/SettingsAiUsageTab.tsx` |\n| `audit` | Audit | `SettingsAiAuditTab` | `.../components/SettingsAiAuditTab.tsx` |\n\n> Note: a **Usage tab already exists** (`usage`, `IconChartBar`, rendered at line 145 via `SettingsAiUsageTab`). It gates on enterprise + ClickHouse and reuses `modules/settings/usage/*`. Per-user drilldown is a separate route: `SettingsPath.AiUsageUserDetail` → `pages/settings/ai/SettingsAiUsageUserDetail.tsx`.\n\n### Providers page (US-127)\n- **`packages/twenty-front/src/pages/settings/ai/SettingsAiProviders.tsx`** — `export const SettingsAiProviders` (line 41). Standalone sub-page (not a tab). Title `t\\`AI providers\\``, breadcrumb `Workspace / Syna / Providers`.\n- Renders `SettingsAiProvidersList` (`components/SettingsAiProvidersList.tsx`) + add/edit `SettingsAiProviderForm`.\n- Data layer:\n  - `pages/settings/ai/hooks/useWorkspaceAiProviders.ts` — `useWorkspaceAiProviders` (query `GET_WORKSPACE_AI_PROVIDERS`, mutations upsert/remove/test).\n  - `pages/settings/ai/graphql/queries/getWorkspaceAiProviders.ts` (query `WorkspaceAiProviders`)\n  - `.../graphql/mutations/{upsertWorkspaceAiProvider,removeWorkspaceAiProvider,testWorkspaceAiProvider}.ts`\n  - `.../types/WorkspaceAiProviderStatus.ts` — `WorkspaceAiProviderStatus`, `WorkspaceAiProvidersOverview`.\n\n### Where tabs/routes are registered\n- **Sidebar nav:** `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/hooks/useSettingsNavigationItems.tsx` lines 171–185. `Syna` item → `SettingsPath.AI`, `IconSparkles`, hidden unless `permissionMap[PermissionFlagType.AI_SETTINGS]`; nested `Providers` subItem → `SettingsPath.AiProviders` (indent level 2). Exported `useSettingsNavigationItems`.\n- **Routes:** `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/app/components/SettingsRoutes.tsx`\n  - Lazy imports: `SettingsAI` (line 253), `SettingsAiProviders` (line 259), `SettingsAiUsageUserDetail` (line 265), `SettingsToolDetail` (line 271), `SettingsAgentForm` (369), `SettingsAgentTurnDetail` (375), `SettingsSkillForm` (381), `SettingsAiPrompts` (387).\n  - AI route group wrapped by `SettingsProtectedRouteWrapper settingsPermission={PermissionFlagType.AI_SETTINGS}` (lines 814–859): `AI`, `AiProviders`, `AiPrompts`, `AiNewAgent`, `AiAgentDetail`, `AiAgentTurnDetail`, `AiNewSkill`, `AiSkillDetail`, `AiUsageUserDetail`, `AiToolDetail`, `LogicFunctionDetail`.\n- **Tab state:** `modules/settings/components/layout/useSettingsActiveTabId.ts` — `useSettingsActiveTabId(componentInstanceId, tabIds)`; resolves URL hash first (deep-link), else stored `activeTabIdComponentState`, else first tab.\n\n### How to add a new tab (e.g. a future \"Usage\"/any tab) within Syna\n1. Add id to `SETTINGS_AI_TABS.TABS_IDS` (`constants/SettingsAiTabs.ts`).\n2. Add an entry to the `tabs` array in `SettingsAI.tsx` (lines 40–71) with `{ id, title: t\\`…\\`, Icon }`.\n3. Add an `isXTab` boolean from `resolvedTabId` and a `{isXTab && <SettingsXTab />}` line (lines 78–83, 141–146).\n4. Optionally add an `actionButton` branch (lines 94–113).\nDeep-links use the hash: `getSettingsPath(SettingsPath.AI, undefined, undefined, 'usage')` (see `modules/settings/usage/components/SettingsUsageAnalyticsSection.tsx:101`).\n\n### How to add a standalone page (e.g. a \"Usage\" page like Providers)\n1. Add enum value to `SettingsPath` (`packages/twenty-shared/src/types/SettingsPath.ts`) e.g. `AiUsage = 'ai/usage'`.\n2. Create the page under `pages/settings/ai/`.\n3. Add a `lazy(() => import(...))` in `SettingsRoutes.tsx` and a `<Route path={SettingsPath.AiUsage} element={...} />` inside the `AI_SETTINGS` group (lines 814–859).\n4. Add a nav entry/subItem in `useSettingsNavigationItems.tsx` (lines 176–184 pattern) if it should appear in the sidebar.\n`getSettingsPath` (`packages/twenty-shared/src/utils/navigation/getSettingsPath.ts`) builds `/{AppPath.Settings}/{to}` with optional params/query/hash.\n\n---\n\n## 2. AI assistant surfaces\n\n### Side panel\n- **`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/side-panel/pages/ask-ai/components/SidePanelAskAiPage.tsx`** — `export const SidePanelAskAiPage` (line 11). Wraps `<AiChatTab />` in `AiChatSurfaceContext.Provider value={AI_CHAT_SURFACE.SIDE_PANEL}`.\n- **Registered:** `modules/side-panel/constants/SidePanelPagesConfig.tsx:61` → `[SidePanelPages.AskAI, <SidePanelAskAiPage />]`.\n- **Enum:** `packages/twenty-shared/src/types/SidePanelPages.ts:20` → `AskAI = 'ask-ai'` (`Copilot` line 11 deprecated → maps to AskAI).\n- **Expand to full page:** `modules/side-panel/pages/ask-ai/hooks/useExpandAskAiSidePanelPage.ts` — `useExpandAskAiSidePanelPage` → `useOpenAiChatPage`.\n\n### Entry points\n- **`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/side-panel/hooks/useOpenAskAiPageInSidePanel.ts`** — `useOpenAskAiPageInSidePanel` (line 13), returns `openAskAiPage({ resetNavigationStack })`; navigates `SidePanelPages.AskAI`, pageTitle `t\\`Syna\\``, `IconSparkles`. Used by command-menu hotkey: `modules/command-menu/hooks/useCommandMenuHotKeys.ts:16,47`.\n- **`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ai/hooks/useOpenAskAiPageWithPreprompt.ts`** — `useOpenAskAiPageWithPreprompt` (line 14), returns `openAskAiPageWithPreprompt({ text, mode='PREFILL', model?: 'FAST'|'SMART' })`; switches to new chat, optionally preselects `currentWorkspace.fastModel`, then `stageAiChatPreprompt`. Callers:\n  - `modules/blocknote-editor/components/SynaSlashMenuItem.tsx:7,42,61`\n  - `modules/front-components/hooks/useFrontComponentExecutionContext.ts:26,141,366` (maps legacy `SidePanelPages.Copilot` → `AskAI`)\n  - `modules/object-record/record-index/hooks/useOpenRecordFromIndexView.ts:122`\n- **Full page:** `pages/ai-chat/AiChatPage.tsx` — `export const AiChatPage`; route `AppPath.AiChat = '/chat/:threadId?'` (`twenty-shared/src/types/AppPath.ts:22`), registered in `modules/app/routing/utils/createWorkspaceRouteObjects.tsx:147-153`. Opened via `modules/ai/hooks/useOpenAiChatPage.ts` (`openAiChatPage`).\n\n### `modules/ai` component structure (selected)\n- `components/AiChatTab.tsx` — `AiChatTab` (core chat: `AiChatTabMessageList`, `AiChatQueuedMessages`, `AiChatEditorSection`).\n- `components/AiChatEditorSection.tsx` — `AiChatEditorSection`; no-model banner at lines 193–198.\n- `components/AiChatEmptyState.tsx`, `AiChatApiKeyNotConfiguredMessage.tsx`, `AiChatBanner.tsx`, `AIChatNoMoreBillingCreditsBanner.tsx`, `AiChatQuestionCard.tsx`, `AiChatSuggestedPrompts`, `AgentChatProvider*`, plus many effects.\n- `constants/AiChatSurface.ts` — `AI_CHAT_SURFACE = { PAGE: 'page', SIDE_PANEL: 'side-panel' }`.\n- `contexts/AiChatSurfaceContext`.\n- `hooks/`, `states/`, `graphql/`, `utils/` (≈50 hooks, ≈50 state atoms).\n\n---\n\n## 3. How the front knows AI is available\n\n| Signal | Symbol | File:line |\n|---|---|---|\n| Client model catalog atom | `aiModelsState` (`ClientAiModelConfig[]`) | `modules/client-config/states/aiModelsState.ts:4` |\n| Populated from client config | `setAiModels` | `modules/client-config/hooks/useClientConfig.ts:55` |\n| Enabled/available models | `useWorkspaceAiModelAvailability()` → `{ enabledModels, realModels, useRecommendedModels }` | `modules/ai/hooks/useWorkspaceAiModelAvailability.ts:7` |\n| Workspace fields backing it | `currentWorkspace.enabledAiModelIds`, `useRecommendedModels`, `fastModel`, `smartModel`, `aiAdditionalInstructions` | `modules/auth/states/currentWorkspaceState.ts:39-44` |\n| Permission gate (action) | `useHasPermissionFlag(PermissionFlagType.AI)` | `modules/settings/roles/hooks/useHasPermissionFlag.ts:9` |\n| Permission gate (settings) | `permissionMap[PermissionFlagType.AI_SETTINGS]` / route wrapper | `useSettingsNavigationItems.tsx:175,182`; `SettingsRoutes.tsx:817` |\n| Command-menu gate string | `\"conditionalAvailabilityExpression\": \"permissionFlags.AI\"` | `testing/mock-data/.../mock-command-menu-items-data.ts:951,973` |\n| Zero-AI gating util | `getOfferedSynaActions({ hasAiPermissionFlag, hasAvailableModel, ... })` | `modules/ai/utils/getOfferedSynaActions.ts:10,21` |\n| Tool index query | `useGetToolIndex()` → `GET_TOOL_INDEX` | `modules/ai/hooks/useGetToolIndex.ts:8`; `modules/ai/graphql/queries/getToolIndex.ts:3` |\n\nModel-availability checks in UI: `AiChatEditorSection.tsx:152-153` (`enabledModels.length === 0` → \"No AI models are enabled…\"), `AiChatQuestionCard.tsx:231-232`, `useAgentChatModelId.ts:10`, `useAiModelOptions.ts:26,37,43`, `SettingsAiModelsTab.tsx:49`. Workspace-unavailable key banner: `AiChatApiKeyNotConfiguredMessage.tsx:22`.\n\nBoth gates are combined for Syna actions (US-130): permission flag **and** an available model, fail-closed (`getOfferedSynaActions.ts` comment + `SynaSlashMenuItem.tsx:28-31`).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Lingui usage pattern\n\nBoth `SettingsAiOverviewTab` and `SettingsAiProviders` use the **macro `t`** with tagged-template literals:\n\n```ts\n// SettingsAiOverviewTab.tsx:11\nimport { t } from '@lingui/core/macro';\n...\n<H2Title\n  title={t`At a glance`}\n  description={t`What's installed and being used in your workspace`}\n/>\n...\nenqueueErrorSnackBar({ message: t`Failed to save workspace instructions` });   // :73\n```\n\n```ts\n// SettingsAiProviders.tsx:3\nimport { t } from '@lingui/core/macro';\n...\nenqueueErrorSnackBar({ message: t`Unable to save the provider` });   // :123\nenqueueSuccessSnackBar({ message: t`Provider saved` });              // :118\ndescription={t`Add and test a provider key, then pick the default and fast model.`}  // :173\n```\n\nVariants in the same area:\n- `SettingsAiProviderForm.tsx` imports both `t` (`@lingui/core/macro`) and `Trans` (`@lingui/react/macro`).\n- Components needing runtime translation use `const { t } = useLingui();` (`@lingui/react/macro`) — e.g. `SettingsAgentSettingsTab.tsx:2,68`, `SettingsAgentToolsTable.tsx:9,47`.\n- `SettingsAiUsageUserDetail.tsx:10-18` uses `import { Trans, useLingui }` and `const { t: tLingui } = useLingui();`.\n- No `msg\\`` usage found in these files; the dominant pattern is `t\\`…\\`` macro (zero-arg interpolation works inline, e.g. `t\\`${providerStatus.availableModelCount} models available\\``).\n\n---\n\n## 5. `SettingsPath` enum & how `AiProviders` was added\n\n**`packages/twenty-shared/src/types/SettingsPath.ts`** (relevant block, lines 40–49):\n\n```ts\nexport enum SettingsPath {\n  ...\n  AI = 'ai',\n  AiProviders = 'ai/providers',\n  AiUsageUserDetail = 'ai/usage/user/:userWorkspaceId',\n  AiPrompts = 'ai/prompts',\n  AiNewAgent = 'ai/new-agent',\n  AiAgentDetail = 'ai/agents/:agentId',\n  AiAgentTurnDetail = 'ai/agents/:agentId/turns/:turnId',\n  AiNewSkill = 'ai/new-skill',\n  AiSkillDetail = 'ai/skills/:skillId',\n  AiToolDetail = 'ai/tools/:toolIdentifier',\n  ...\n}\n```\n\n`AiProviders = 'ai/providers'` was added as a child path of the existing `AI = 'ai'`. Consumers:\n- Route: `SettingsRoutes.tsx:822-825` (`<Route path={SettingsPath.AiProviders} element={<SettingsAiProviders />} />`).\n- Nav: `useSettingsNavigationItems.tsx:179` (`path: SettingsPath.AiProviders`, nested subItem).\n- Breadcrumbs: `SettingsAiProviders.tsx:156-157`.\nAdding a new settings sub-page therefore means appending an enum member here first (it's the shared source of truth imported by both front and server-side `getSettingsPath`).\n\n---\n\n## 6. \"Connect a provider\" / \"configure provider\" empty-state copy\n\nThere is **no \"Connect a provider\" copy** anywhere in the front (grep for `Connect a provider|connect provider|Add a provider|No provider configured|configure a provider` returned no matches). Existing provider-related copy:\n\n- **`SettingsAiProviders.tsx:183-189`** — section for adding one:\n```tsx\n<H2Title\n  title={t`OpenAI-compatible endpoint`}\n  description={t`Connect any self-hosted or proxy endpoint that speaks the OpenAI API.`}\n/>\n<Button title={t`Add OpenAI-compatible provider`} Icon={IconPlus} onClick={handleAddOpenAiCompatible} />\n```\n- **`SettingsAiProvidersList.tsx:35,86`** — row description/status: `t\\`No API key configured\\``, `t\\`Configured\\`` / `t\\`No key\\``, source labels `Workspace key` / `Instance` / `Catalog` (lines 20-25). When `providers` is empty it renders an empty `SettingsListCard` — no dedicated empty-state message.\n- **`SettingsAiAuditTab.tsx:108-111`** — `t\\`No providers configured\\`` (value `\"—\"`).\n- **`SettingsAiProviderForm.tsx:95-99`** — `t\\`Add an OpenAI-compatible provider: any endpoint speaking the OpenAI API.\\`` / `t\\`The workspace key overrides the instance and catalog configuration for this provider.\\``\n- **`SettingsAiOverviewTab.tsx:114-117`** — `t\\`MCP Server\\`` + `t\\`Connect AI assistants like Claude or Cursor to your workspace via the Model Context Protocol\\`` / `Set up MCP`.\n- **`SettingsAgentSettingsTab.tsx:136`** — `t\\`No models available. Please configure AI models in your workspace settings.\\``\n- **`AiChatApiKeyNotConfiguredMessage.tsx:22`** — `t\\`AI not configured. Set OPENAI_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, or XAI_API_KEY…\\``.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Audit tab front component & its query\n\n- **Component:** `packages/twenty-front/src/pages/settings/ai/components/SettingsAiAuditTab.tsx` — `export const SettingsAiAuditTab` (line 23). Rendered by `SettingsAI.tsx:146` when the `audit` tab is active.\n- **Query:** `useEventLogs` from `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/event-logs/hooks/useQueryEventLogs.ts` (line 19), which calls GraphQL `GET_EVENT_LOGS`:\n```ts\n// SettingsAiAuditTab.tsx:37-41\nconst { records, totalCount, hasNextPage, loading, error, loadMore } =\n  useEventLogs(\n    { table: EventLogTable.USAGE_EVENT, first: AI_AUDIT_LOG_PAGE_SIZE }, // AI_AUDIT_LOG_PAGE_SIZE = 50\n    { skip: !canQueryUsageLogs },\n  );\n```\n- **GraphQL doc:** `modules/settings/event-logs/graphql/queries/getEventLogs.ts` — `GET_EVENT_LOGS` query `EventLogs($input: EventLogQueryInput!) { eventLogs(input: $input) { records { event timestamp userId properties recordId objectMetadataId } totalCount pageInfo { endCursor hasNextPage } } }`.\n- **Gating:** `canQueryUsageLogs = isClickHouseConfigured && hasAuditLogsEntitlement` (lines 28–35); `hasAuditLogsEntitlement` checks `currentWorkspace.billingEntitlements` for `BillingEntitlementKey.AUDIT_LOGS`. Fallbacks render `SettingsEnterpriseFeatureGateCard`, a ClickHouse notice, or an error container (lines 45–98).\n- **Other UI:** provider credential masks section uses `getAiProviderCredentialStatuses(aiModels)` → `pages/settings/ai/utils/getAiProviderCredentialStatuses.ts` (fixed mask `'••••••••'`, never a real secret); logs table is `modules/settings/event-logs/components/EventLogResultsTable.tsx`. Test: `pages/settings/ai/components/__tests__/SettingsAiAuditTab.test.tsx`.\n\n---\n\n### Quick path index\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/hooks/useSettingsNavigationItems.tsx`\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/app/components/SettingsRoutes.tsx`\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/pages/settings/ai/SettingsAI.tsx`\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/pages/settings/ai/SettingsAiProviders.tsx`\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/pages/settings/ai/constants/SettingsAiTabs.ts`\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/pages/settings/ai/components/SettingsAi{Overview,Audit,Usage,Models}Tab.tsx`\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/side-panel/pages/ask-ai/components/SidePanelAskAiPage.tsx`\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/side-panel/hooks/useOpenAskAiPageInSidePanel.ts`\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ai/hooks/useOpenAskAiPageWithPreprompt.ts`\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ai/hooks/useWorkspaceAiModelAvailability.ts`\n- `packages/twenty-shared/src/types/SettingsPath.ts`\n- `packages/twenty-shared/src/types/SidePanelPages.ts`\n\nNo files were modified.\n</task_result>\n</task>"
